             82  *      EXTENDED COMMAND HANDLER FORMAT
             83  *
             84  *           1000 *COMMAND_NAME parameters
             85  *                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^
             86  *      EPROM FORMAT
             87  *
             88  *           DATA >9C42        IDENTIFIER WORD
             89  *           DATA LINK1        LINK TO NEXT DIR. ENTRY
             90  *           DATA ENTRY1       ENTRY PT. OF COMMAND_1 ROUTINE
             91  *           TEXT 'COMMAND_1'  NAME
             92  *           BYTE 0            TERMINATOR FOR NAME
             93  *   LINK1   DATA LINK2        LINK TO NEXT DIR. ENTRY
             94  *           DATA ENTRY2       ENTRY PT. OF COMMAND_2 ROUTINE
             95  *           TEXT 'CPMMAND_2'  NAME
             96  *           BYTE 0            TERMINATOR FOR NAME
             97  *   LINK2   DATA 0            LINK TERMINATOR !!
             98  *
             99  *   EXTENDED COMMAND HANDLERS ARE LOCATED ON 4K BYTE
            100  *   BOUNDARIES STARTING FROM >010000 AND ARE MAPPED INTO
            101  *   THE CPU ADDRESS SPACE FROM >2000 TO >3FFF. ALL EXTENDED
            102  *   COMMAND HANDLER EPROMS MUST BE INSTALLED BETWEEN
            103  *   >01 0000 AND >0F FFFF
            104  *
